rticle class=\"post-card\">\\n            <p class=\"meta\">January 2025 · Data integration</p>\\n            <h3><a href=\"#single-cell-genomics\">Bridging Machine Learning and Single-Cell Genomics</a></h3>\\n            <p>Lessons from building scalable pipelines for multimodal single-cell genomics and spatial transcriptomics.</p>\\n          </article>\\n          <article class=\"post-card\">\\n            <p class=\"meta\">November 2024 · Connectomics</p>\\n            <h3><a href=\"#connectomics\">Scaling Graph Neural Networks for Connectomics</a></h3>\\n            <p>Practical notes on graph construction, motif discovery, and collaboration between model developers and microscopy teams.</p>\\n          </article>\\n        </div>\\n      </section>\\n\\n      <section class=\"section muted\" aria-label=\"Blog summaries\">\\n        <div class=\"container\">\\n          <article id=\"interpretable-deep-learning\" class=\"feature-article\">\\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">March 2025</p>\\n            <h2>Building Interpretable Deep Learning Models for Neuroscience</h2>\\n            <p>Interpretable neural decoders require more than strong predictive performance. Our lab evaluates feature attributions, stability across recording sessions, and alignment with known circuit physiology before using models to generate hypotheses.</p>\\n          </article>\\n          <article id=\"single-cell-genomics\" class=\"feature-article\">\\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">January 2025</p>\\n            <h2>Bridging Machine Learning and Single-Cell Genomics</h2>\\n            <p>Single-cell projects succeed when data engineering, statistical modeling, and biological interpretation are designed together. CellMap reflects this by combining reproducible workflows with Bayesian clustering and careful visual review.</p>\\n          </article>\\n          <article id=\"connectomics\" class=\"feature-article\">\\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">November 2024</p>\\n            <h2>Scaling Graph Neural Networks for Connectomics</h2>\\n            <p>Connectomics graphs are large, noisy, and richly structured. NeuroGraph focuses on robust graph representations that help researchers classify synapses and compare connectivity motifs across datasets.</p>\\n   "]
